Migrate `Net::Async::MCP::Server` from MCP 2025-11-25 to **2026-07-28** (the
spec revision that ships with the Perl `MCP` distribution 0.15). 2026-07-28
is a **breaking change release** — the protocol becomes fully stateless, the
`initialize` handshake is removed, and every request carries `protocolVersion`
and `clientCapabilities` in `_meta`.

# Why

The Perl `MCP` distribution 0.15 (released 2026-07-30) aligns with the
2026-07-28 spec, which deprecates the session-based protocol we currently
implement. Without this migration, every wire payload we accept from a
2026-07-28 client is silently wrong; the cpanfile bump alone is not
sufficient — the protocol interpretation must follow.

# Spec references

- [2026-07-28 spec root](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28)
- [Changelog 2025-11-25 → 2026-07-28](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/changelog)
- [Base protocol overview](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/index)
- [Stdio transport](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio)

# Goal

1. Protocol version string → `2026-07-28`.
2. Every request parsed for `_meta` with `io.modelcontextprotocol/*` keys.
3. Every result carries `resultType` (and `io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo` in `_meta`).
4. `tools/list` results carry `ttlMs` and `cacheScope`.
5. `tools/call` results wrapped in MCP content blocks.
6. `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, `ping`, `logging/setLevel`,
   `notifications/roots/list_changed` removed.
7. `server/discover` RPC added.
8. New error codes: `-32020 HeaderMismatch`, `-32021 MissingRequiredClientCapability`,
   `-32022 UnsupportedProtocolVersion`.
9. MRTR (Multi Round-Trip Requests) shape: `InputRequiredResult` with
   `resultType: "input_required"` and `inputRequests`.
10. Stdio transport is stateless: one line per request, no session, no handshake.
    EOF on stdin = graceful shutdown.
11. `server/discover` is the new pre-flight RPC; clients may call it
    before any other request for up-front version selection.

# Subtasks

1. **Drop the initialize handshake.** Remove `initialize`,
   `notifications/initialized`, `ping` handling. The discovery step becomes
   `server/discover`. (`handle()` rejects `initialize` with `-32601` going
   forward; do not silently no-op.)
2. **Per-request `_meta` parsing.** New top-of-`handle()` block extracts
   `io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion`, `/clientInfo`, `/clientCapabilities`,
   `/logLevel`. The protocol version is required; missing → `-32602 Invalid params`.
   Unsupported version → `-32022 UnsupportedProtocolVersion` with `supported: [...]`
   payload. Missing required capability → `-32021 MissingRequiredClientCapability`.
3. **Per-result `_meta` injection.** Every successful result includes
   `resultType: "complete"` and `io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo` in `_meta`.
   The `_meta` injection is part of `_jsonrpc_response`, not the caller.
4. **`server/discover` RPC.** Returns
   `{ supportedVersions: ["2026-07-28"], capabilities, serverInfo, extensions }`.
   Available before any other request — useful for stdio as a backward-compat
   probe, and for HTTP as a pre-flight.
5. **`tools/list` result shape.**
   `{ tools: [...], resultType: "complete", ttlMs, cacheScope, _meta: { ... } }`.
   Each tool definition uses `inputSchema` (camelCase) — karr #3.
6. **`tools/call` content blocks.** Wrap success return in
   `{ content: [{ type: "text", text: ... }], resultType: "complete" }`.
   Tool errors → JSON-RPC error with `-32602 Invalid params` (legacy `-32002`
   still accepted on input).
7. **MRTR-ready `call_tool`.** When a tool needs more input, return
   `InputRequiredResult` with `resultType: "input_required"` and
   `inputRequests`. Stub for now; wire parity is the goal.
8. **New error codes.** Add `-32020 HeaderMismatch`, `-32021 MissingRequiredClientCapability`,
   `-32022 UnsupportedProtocolVersion` to `_jsonrpc_error`. Drop the `ping` path.
9. **Stdio transport.** One line per request, no session, no handshake.
   `handle_requests` exits on EOF. Blocking IO is acceptable per spec.
10. **Configure / constructor.** Apply karr #6 — `configure` should accept
    (or at least surface) unknown params, not silently drop them. Keep the
    `name` shortcut. Validate `inputSchema` keys exist on the tool definition.
11. **Tests.** Update `t/01-basic.t` and add `t/02-protocol-2026-07-28.t`
    covering:
      - `_meta` parsing (valid, missing required keys, wrong version)
      - `server/discover`
      - `tools/list` shape (`resultType`, `ttlMs`, `cacheScope`)
      - `tools/call` content blocks
      - MRTR `input_required` shape
      - error codes (-32020, -32021, -32022, -32602)
      - notification POST returns 202 (HTTP) / no-op (stdio)
      - initialize is rejected with `-32601`
      - ping is rejected with `-32601`

