- #1 Stdio blocks loop — partially addressed by subtask 9 (stateless, ephemeral).
  Native `IO::Async::Stream` integration is a stretch goal within this ticket.
- #2 Tool errors → JSON-RPC errors — addressed in subtask 6.
- #3 input_schema → inputSchema — addressed in subtask 5.
- #4 tools/call content blocks — addressed in subtask 6.
- #5 initialize protocolVersion — addressed in subtask 1 (initialize is removed).
- #6 configure unknown params — addressed in subtask 10.
- #7 handle() unused context — replaced by the per-request `_meta` block in subtask 2.
- #8 README drift — fold into the documentation ticket; do not duplicate here.

# Out of scope

- Streamable HTTP transport (separate ticket).
- Tasks extension (`io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks`).
- Logging (deprecated; server logs to stderr).
- Roots / Sampling (deprecated in 2026-07-28).
- Multi-server `extensions` capability negotiation.
- Backwards-compatibility fallback for 2025-11-25 clients. Decision: **not
  supported** in 0.002. Add a `Changes` note. A future ticket can add
  era-detection if needed.

# Definition of done

- All existing tests adapted to the new protocol.
- New `t/02-protocol-2026-07-28.t` covers the wire format end-to-end.
- `prove -l t/` passes.
- `dzil build` succeeds.
- `Changes` has a 0.002 entry with the breaking-change note.
- `dist.ini` still uses `[@Author::GETTY]`; no new bundle plugins needed.
- `cpanfile` updated for any new runtime deps (none expected, since the
  migration is architecture-only).
## Done (2026-08-16)

All 11 subtasks landed. Files: lib/Net/Async/MCP/Server.pm, lib/Net/Async/MCP/Server/Transport/Stdio.pm, t/01-basic.t, t/02-protocol-2026-07-28.t (new), Changes.

Verify: prove -l t/ (30 tests, all pass) and dzil test (32 tests including author/release, all pass or skipped-as-release-only). dzil build succeeded.

Spec choices made:
- ttlMs default: 300000 (5 min) on tools/list and server/discover, matching the spec example.
- cacheScope default: 'public' on tools/list and server/discover (tools are typically identical across users).
- input_schema is still accepted at register_tool() and normalised to inputSchema, so callers migrating incrementally don't break.
- Tool execution errors become isError: true content blocks (model-recoverable, per spec); unknown-tool errors stay as -32602 JSON-RPC errors.

Folded: #1 (partial via statelessness), #2, #3, #4, #5, #6, #7. Untouched: #8 (karr #11), #10 (HTTP), #11.
